{"kind":"stack","id":"stack-circuits-switch","title":"Switches and circuits: does the lamp light?","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1f2937","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Switch"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A part you turn on or off to open or close a circuit."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Closed circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A complete loop with no gaps, so electricity can flow and a lamp lights."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"When a switch is turned on, what happens to the circuit?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"It is closed, so the lamp lights","why":"A closed switch completes the loop so current flows.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"It is open, so the lamp lights","why":"Pupils mix up open and closed; an open circuit has a gap.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"It is open, so the lamp goes out","why":"Pupils think the switch must be on to stop the lamp.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which word means a broken loop with a gap in it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Open circuit","why":"An open circuit has a gap, so current cannot flow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Closed circuit","why":"Pupils confuse closed with broken; closed means complete.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Full circuit","why":"Pupils think a full battery means a complete loop.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Ella has a battery, wires and a lamp. Which path should she take?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Connect the switch in the loop","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Leave a gap in the wire","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Ella turns the switch on. The lamp lights. Good choice!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The gap stops the flow. The lamp stays dark. Try again next time!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"A switch is open. Does the lamp in a series circuit light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"No, the lamp stays off","why":"An open switch leaves a gap, so no current flows.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Yes, the lamp lights","why":"Pupils think a battery alone makes a lamp light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Only if the battery is new","why":"Pupils think battery age matters more than the loop.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"In a series circuit, what does closing the switch do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Completes the loop so the lamp lights","why":"Closing the switch joins the gap, letting current flow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Uses up the battery straight away","why":"Pupils think a switch drains the battery when closed.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Makes the lamp dimmer","why":"Pupils think the switch changes brightness rather than flow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"How many lamps light if one lamp is removed from a series loop?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"None, the loop is broken","why":"Removing a lamp breaks the loop, so no current flows.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"All of them still light","why":"Pupils think each lamp has its own separate supply.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Only the battery lights","why":"Pupils think the battery is a lamp in the loop.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You know how switches control circuits."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Keep exploring circuits and see which path lights the lamp."}],"actions":[]}}
